The paper confirms the key fork: general \(b^\*\)-coloring is NP-complete even on co-bipartite graphs (Section 2), while trees, block graphs, cacti, and \(P_4\)-sparse graphs have explicit polynomial structure. A planted coloring on an arbitrary random graph would not inherit the paper’s worst-case hardness, so I’m not treating that triage idea as Track A evidence. I’m now testing whether the paper’s polynomial block/cactus construction supports an honest Track B family with a large mechanical/compact-route gap.
